                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "231549611",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198349857022",
                            "num_reviews": 354,
                            "playtime_forever": 82,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 82,
                            "last_played": 1785279578
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1] Funny Little Game [/h1]\n\nShadow of Loot Box is a perfectly adequate little game that pokes fun at the shortcomings of modern gaming. Despite being nearly a decade old, everything it makes fun of is still very much prevalent in today's games, if not even more so. The shooting and combat in the game isn't very great, as it's pretty stiff and repetitive. but that's not really the point of the game. Each level pokes fun at something, whether it be a buggy level full of glitches, a level that's laggy due to DRM, or an escort level with a partner that liked to wander off, most levels were short enough to be able to enjoy whatever was being mocked without overstaying their welcome. The game isn't incredible, but I had a fun time with it and I don't think it overstays its welcome. For $5, it's good for a little laugh. For more reviews, follow my [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/40795588-Eggroll-Recommends/] curator page. [/url]",
